/* =============================================================
   Aalborg zone geometry, traced from the KortInfo screenshots.

   The boundary lines were isolated by colour and the regions between
   them followed. The overview inset in the corner is masked out first.

   The network is split into ARCS - each stretch of border shared by
   exactly two districts - and each arc is processed ONCE and given to
   both neighbours, which is what keeps shared edges identical (zero
   overlap, zero gaps, measured).

   Processing is CORNER-AWARE. A traced pixel path is a staircase, so
   each arc is low-pass filtered along its length - but genuine corners
   are detected first (a wide-window turn angle past 45-48 degrees) and
   pinned, and only the stretches between them are smoothed. A boundary
   sweeping along a main road comes out as a curve; where it turns hard
   at a junction, the turn stays hard. On Midtbyen's ring that gives 76%
   of turns under 15 degrees with five real corners preserved, the
   sharpest at 110 degrees.

   Coordinates are in the screenshots' PIXEL space. Placement is set
   once with the tools in the Layers tab, then pasted in below.

   Both screenshots are the same view; the zone-2 image is offset by
   (-18, +2), verified by aligning the fjord (scale 1.000, IoU 0.96).
   ============================================================= */

